A||||6||BAM-BAM||Headers?? Yes? Or No?||||12||
Z||000000||BAM-BAM||04-24-2001||12:59 AM||||  With all the discussion lately about headers, I am begining to wonder if it's all for naught. Most seem to think that for the money, there are no real power gains. Please feel free to correct me if I'm wrong. I will be running a 3.4 in a 85GT auto. I may or may not be running performance heads. But little else internaly will change. LMK. TIA<P>Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>Knowledge is POWER!<BR>That is why the ignorant remain Weak!||||reg||12
Z||000001||kitcar||04-24-2001||01:23 AM||||I dont know if this wil help you out but its worth a try...It really matters on what kind of headers you decide to get.  Make sure you look into all the peformance headers made for your engine, and compare them.  Also check the tourq and HP gains. <P>I also have a 2000 trans am, and i installed MAC headers on it, and it made a WORLD of a diff.  I was running 13 flat, now im hitting best of 12.6.  But i have no traction on the car, and have raced a guy that ran 12.1 on a roll and won.  Headers is made for long gains, not for the start.<P>I think you will me impressed with them, just as long as you make sure of the quailty and gains of it.  Make sure it provides good prof!<P>just my .02||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||04-24-2001||01:41 AM||||Of course this is just my opinion and I have no "real" data, But I have noticed a world of difference when I installed my Sprints. The actual gains may not be that big number wise, as for driveability, it is much better. I would also think that on a larger volume engine (3.4 as compared to a 2.8) the headers/performance manifolds would provide a higher gain. Although the cost is high, I would most likely still buy them if I had to do it over. I have had mine for over 5 years and had no problems. I know folks that had their stock ones ported and re-welded and still had cracks develop over the years.||||reg||1
Z||000003||WKDFIRO||04-24-2001||03:21 AM||||Primarily I have been looking at headers to replace the cracking manifolds more than performance peaks. It can be disheartening to put a manifold in the front knowing that there is absolutely no garantee that I wouldn't be doing it again next year. ||||reg||6
Z||000004||1FST2M6||04-24-2001||08:05 AM||||on a 3.4 anything is better than the stock manifold. the added displacement with have HELLA backpressure which will kill any HP you may have... you've seen my dyno sheets.. i'd go with <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A>  's shorty headers. better than stock and not as radical as the long tube units. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||BAM-BAM||04-24-2001||08:08 AM||||  Thanks for the info. I will keep looking around ans see what's available. Are Chris West, Fiero Store and Focoa The only headrers available for the stock exhaust? LMK. TIA<P>Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000006||Carrolles||04-24-2001||08:16 AM||||With three daughters in college and a wedding coming up later this year cost is an issue for me.  I'm very pleased with the results of porting the intake and exhaust manifolds on my 85SE v-6 4spd.<P>I'd love to try headers but my Grooms 2.8 rebuild just doesn't justify the expense.  Maybe later if I do a 3.4 swap.||||reg||1
